From 23c0d272e918c7c8c7728bd5076df0913f5a745e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 20:48:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03708/11362] [outer-loop] Multi-level deepening diag: the 0.0
 wall is a HARNESS ARTIFACT; stall is in INDUCTION not exploration

Operator: "let's iterate on multi-level live deepening." Diagnosed WHERE L1->L2 fails
before proposing a lever. Findings:

1. HEADLINE: live_multi_level_solve_rate=0.0 is a MEASUREMENT ARTIFACT. exp4646 divides
   depth>=2/all attempts, but its source rollout (experiment_4628.run_variant_attempt)
   BREAKS at the first level-up with target_levels=1, capping reached_level at start+1 ->
   depth>=2 structurally impossible -> 0.0 regardless of capability. The .429 generation
   levers will be judged against a metric that cannot move.

2. Exploration ALONE never deepens (proto_multilevel_diag_noop, 9 games, budget 3000,
   target_levels=5, no break): 0/9 reach L2; the 3 reaching L1 explore 460-1843 more
   states without finding L2. Explorer is not the bottleneck; goal/rule INDUCTION is.

3. Real LLM induction (proto_multilevel_diag_real, lp85) FIRES at the L1 boundary
   (induced=True, 792 transitions, 176s) but yields plan_len=0 -- no L2 plan, falls back to
   explore, stays at L1. Caveats: proposer port 8919 collided with a persistent gemma-4-12B
   server (induction ran on gemma not Qwen; conservative + a real local-measurement bug);
   n=1 game.

Recommendation: fix the metric harness (target_levels>=2 + no break + correct proposer
port) before the .429 levers can register; the wall is induction at the L1->L2 boundary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
